	<body id="top">
			<header id="header">
				<a href="#" class="image avatar"><img src="http://s.gravatar.com/avatar/aa975917c25a92b435387bbfd06c34d2?s=200" alt="" /></a>
				<h1><strong>I am Sam Wood</strong>.<br />
			</header>
			<div id="main">
					<section id="one">
						<header class="major">
							<h2><b>Neo</b>&bullet;<i>philiac</i>. [n]<h3><blockquote>“The trait of being excited and pleased by novelty...”<br>&mdash;The New Hacker's Dictionary</blockquote></h3></h2>
						</header>
						<p>January 22, 2016. Mountain View, CA.</p>
						<p>Hello! I strive for meaningful impact through invention and the application of transformative technology.   I’m presently a distributed systems researcher, software engineer, entrepreneur, DJ, husband, and father. My active work topics include mesh networking, cryptocurrencies, and nondualism philosophy.</p>
						<p>I received my B.S. in Computer Science from UC San Diego, cum laude, with a focus on web application development and novel database frameworks. I received my M.S. in Computer Engineering from UC Santa Cruz (<a href="https://ccrg.soe.ucsc.edu">CCRG lab</a>), and <a href="SamWood-MastersThesis.pdf">my thesis</a> details a novel network coding routing and caching system for delay tolerant networks. Under the DARPA <a href="http://arstechnica.com/information-technology/2013/09/darpa-reinvents-peer-to-peer-for-battlefield-with-tactical-torrents/">CBMEN</a> program I authored several peer-reviewed papers that describe novel algorithms for communication in information centric networks, which were successfully implemented and evaluated in field demonstrations. I have a history of leading small teams to deliver high risk, high reward projects under short time frames. I have previously worked for Yahoo! (Strategic Data Solutions), Apple (iTunes Music Store), SRI International (<a href="http://www.csl.sri.com">Computer Science Laboratory</a>), and Tesla Motors. I have also worked for several smaller startups, including an IT company in Bangalore India in 2009.
						<p>I hold a 2nd degree black belt in Shaolin Kempo and actively practice yoga. My <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Erdős_number">Erdős number</a> is 4 [1]. I occasionally run event production and DJ for family gatherings and <a href="http://www.clubconscious.org">ecstatic</a> <a href="http://www.clubconscious.org">dance</a> within the Bay Area. I have volunteered for the Town of Los Altos Hills emergency preparedness and disaster response team. My ham radio call sign is KG6HMQ.
						<br/>
						<br/>
						[1] Via <a herf="https://users.soe.ucsc.edu/~avg/">Allen Van Gelder</a>, Jeff Ullman, and Ron Graham.
						<br/>
